  "id": "behavioral-self-control-training",
  "term": "behavioral self-control training",
  "definition": "Behavioral self-control training is a psychological treatment for alcohol use disorder that aims to help people reduce harmful drinking and work toward controlled drinking rather than only abstinence. In the source packet, it is described as a brief intervention delivered in five sessions and presented as an effective option for treatment-seeking individuals with alcohol use disorder.",
