      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims BSCT “aims to help people reduce harmful drinking.” The packet discusses the goal of “controlled drinking” and the importance of minimizing harmful consumption, but it does not explicitly state that BSCT specifically aims to reduce harmful drinking (as opposed to targeting controlled drinking).",
        "The packet frames BSCT as cost-effective and potentially valuable for targeting controlled drinking, but it does not directly support the broader wording in the first sentence about “rather than only abstinence” as an explicit stated aim of BSCT itself (the abstinence vs controlled-drinking contrast is discussed in the background about treatment goals and uptake)."
